---
title: Betsy — Lifecycle of one procurement decision
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> Detected: pipeline run finds a condition

    Detected --> Evaluated: rank suppliers (evaluate node)
    Evaluated --> Decided: classify the decision (decide node)

    state Decided <<choice>>
    Decided --> AutoApproved: PO total < $5,000 and no anomaly
    Decided --> PendingHumanReview: duplicate invoice / price spike / escalate / PO total >= $5,000

    note right of Decided
        The $5,000 limit (MAX_AUTO_USD) is a hard rule
        in the decide node. The model cannot override it.
    end note

    AutoApproved --> POCreated: act node creates the PO (status: created)

    PendingHumanReview --> POCreated: Jenny approves a generate_po (status: approved)
    PendingHumanReview --> Resolved: Jenny approves a flag (logged, no PO)
    PendingHumanReview --> Rejected: Jenny declines

    POCreated --> InTransit: status -> in_transit
    InTransit --> Delivered: status -> delivered
    Delivered --> ScoreUpdated: EMA updates the supplier's reliability score

    Rejected --> [*]
    Resolved --> [*]
    ScoreUpdated --> [*]
